				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xei4kpuuaogvgnvufre7wvjm/bafkreigphqyvgorv7zyiphugwgccquzbevo7hvxflrujfoy6qhee4o6goy"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T14:19:46.917Z",
			"content": "<p>To prevent the browser from picking the one in the root by default?</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:z6uec3g7xgkvxpy442663waq/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf4owt4k22c",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf3vl5r3c2e",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/kilianvalkhof.com/post/3muf4owt4k22c",
			"author": {
				"name": "Kilian Valkhof",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/kilianvalkhof.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:z6uec3g7xgkvxpy442663waq/bafkreierzj24duh6a4bulcv46iest4pl5zzvbmgrnetuzkd2ff66spv2lq"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T14:31:52.641Z",
			"content": "<p>well, they're a bigcorp so i assume:</p>\n<p>- they needed a way to dynamically serve different favicons (time, locale, events) &amp; it was just easier (for the team, for access mgmt) to build those rules in a js file than elsewhere<br>\n- 'under no circumstance should you show a stale favicon' success criterion.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf5rc5do22p",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf3t5x5j22e",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/duffeh.bsky.social/post/3muf5rc5do22p",
			"author": {
				"name": "Duffeh",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/duffeh.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/bafkreihf42m7kegjr2iu7zucmfcby4dqblokuc7ii3nomjtfv7tod5m6la"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T14:51:05.359Z",
			"content": "<p>Yeah it looks to be what Adobe claim is the \"future of frontend\" called EDS, which is a client side render, for pages that could be static generated.</p>\n<p>They talk a lot about perfect lighthouse score, at what seems like a cost to real users. The header is a tell they load that last for some reason.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf6dx2c522p",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:gvi5yecbeb6e6oc32kbx35jl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mu6cybb4rc2z",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/duffeh.bsky.social/post/3muf6dx2c522p",
			"author": {
				"name": "Duffeh",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/duffeh.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/bafkreihf42m7kegjr2iu7zucmfcby4dqblokuc7ii3nomjtfv7tod5m6la"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T15:01:31.260Z",
			"content": "<p>They do a lot of rubbish like this as a part of their new framework sadly.</p>\n<p>The initial html the LCP image likely has loading='lazy' and in JavaScript they will change it to loading eager to make lighthouse \"happy\".</p>\n<p>Adobe is just a perfect example of what not to do.n</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dmgoddsemnyljdrp4jgt4dam/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf6m2dyis2n",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf6dx2c522p",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mwdelaney.me/post/3muf6m2dyis2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "Michael",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/mwdelaney.me",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dmgoddsemnyljdrp4jgt4dam/bafkreiceamr3su5jnraffld424q2i5vw3dap5aei43qliywmg7glbm6exi"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T15:06:03.159Z",
			"content": "<p>For as long as we've had web technology some people have been desperate to use something, anything else</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufaojee322g",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:z6uec3g7xgkvxpy442663waq/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf4owt4k22c",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3mufaojee322g",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T15:43:13.493Z",
			"content": "<p>yeah, that seems logical (though I disagree with their conclusion 🤔)</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufasti6nc2g",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:spulgjrl7sactd23bgqv6jen/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf5rc5do22p",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3mufasti6nc2g",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T15:45:38.322Z",
			"content": "<p>Huh. 😬</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufezclnhc2l",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:z6uec3g7xgkvxpy442663waq/app.bsky.feed.post/3muf33g736k2j",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me/post/3mufezclnhc2l",
			"author": {
				"name": "Andy Davies",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/bafkreibthta5fiablcbztoiuclttohjox4ilrok6eex2qd42sxvgrhzuny"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T17:00:50.456Z",
			"content": "<p>Unless they’ve actually got a favicon in the root they’ll still get a bunch of 404s as plenty of services on the web go looking for it</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/app.bsky.feed.post/3muffcyhsex27",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufezclnhc2l",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/simoncox.com/post/3muffcyhsex27",
			"author": {
				"name": "SimonCox",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/simoncox.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/bafkreiabali2634y2slw3yiixyfgxibw6qhnvmp6imzbvyuflezvkjg4em"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T17:06:15.335Z",
			"content": "<p>But doesn't the null value of data stop the second request for the favicon?  The page pops up a where to go choice, USA or UK in my case, and when you make a choice the url has a parameter appended and also an actual favicon in the html. It's a a messy solution and i bet the brand teams don't know.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:z6uec3g7xgkvxpy442663waq/app.bsky.feed.post/3muffswgd7s2t",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufezclnhc2l",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/kilianvalkhof.com/post/3muffswgd7s2t",
			"author": {
				"name": "Kilian Valkhof",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/kilianvalkhof.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:z6uec3g7xgkvxpy442663waq/bafkreierzj24duh6a4bulcv46iest4pl5zzvbmgrnetuzkd2ff66spv2lq"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T17:15:10.115Z",
			"content": "<p>I imagine at Adobe scale it matters in terms of pure bandwidth costs even if there are other services also auto fetching.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3muffvee6wk2l",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/app.bsky.feed.post/3muffcyhsex27",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me/post/3muffvee6wk2l",
			"author": {
				"name": "Andy Davies",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/bafkreibthta5fiablcbztoiuclttohjox4ilrok6eex2qd42sxvgrhzuny"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T17:16:31.834Z",
			"content": "<p>Only in a browser… there are many other things that request the default favicon.ico</p>\n<p>And if a site doesn’t have one it’s no that unusual to see them serve a custom 404 page in response!</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3muffydydqc2o",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3muffvee6wk2l",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me/post/3muffydydqc2o",
			"author": {
				"name": "Andy Davies",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/bafkreibthta5fiablcbztoiuclttohjox4ilrok6eex2qd42sxvgrhzuny"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T17:18:12.108Z",
			"content": "<p>Adobe actually has a default favicon.ico</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufij32cgc2g",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3muffvee6wk2l",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/simoncox.com/post/3mufij32cgc2g",
			"author": {
				"name": "SimonCox",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/simoncox.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/bafkreiabali2634y2slw3yiixyfgxibw6qhnvmp6imzbvyuflezvkjg4em"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T18:03:20.642Z",
			"content": "<p>That I did not know and need to read up on! Ta!</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufio7bw4c2g",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3muffydydqc2o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/simoncox.com/post/3mufio7bw4c2g",
			"author": {
				"name": "SimonCox",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/simoncox.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/bafkreiabali2634y2slw3yiixyfgxibw6qhnvmp6imzbvyuflezvkjg4em"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T18:06:12.862Z",
			"content": "<p>Yes. But looks like someone made a decision to only load it after that initial page. I can’t think of a good tech reason other than size of log files and reducing number of times a year a full log brings down servers</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufioftxs22g",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufio7bw4c2g",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/simoncox.com/post/3mufioftxs22g",
			"author": {
				"name": "SimonCox",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/simoncox.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/bafkreiabali2634y2slw3yiixyfgxibw6qhnvmp6imzbvyuflezvkjg4em"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T18:06:19.745Z",
			"content": "<p>or they are hedging in case they need to split the company and change logos - nothing that a cache purge would not sort out though!</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufsll3qyc22",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:tki7vwlanxbwrz2er67eaeqa/app.bsky.feed.post/3mufioftxs22g",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me/post/3mufsll3qyc22",
			"author": {
				"name": "Andy Davies",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/andydavies.me",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ccw4zckt3u7hytoxemgoe654/bafkreibthta5fiablcbztoiuclttohjox4ilrok6eex2qd42sxvgrhzuny"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-31T21:03:41.996Z",
			"content": "<p>First came across it sometime around 2012 Ecotricity has a pair of load balanced servers — one had a favicon and one didn’t</p>\n<p>Don’t come across it as much now but haven’t looked for a while</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		}
